{# Comments under an article. Readers sign in — with Google, Instagram,
   LINE, or email, the same interview session the interview form uses —
   and comment with their real name — no anonymous comments, no made-up
   names. The section is driven by /js/comments.js: it fetches the thread
   from the comments API and renders it. data-comments-api is the API
   base — empty means the same origin (/api on jonathanmccallum.com);
   the preview branch sets it to the test Worker. data-comments-client-id
   is the Google OAuth client id; empty means Google sign-in is not set
   up yet and the list still shows, with a short note instead of the
   sign-in button.
   A comment may carry one optional link to the reader's own social
   profile (Instagram, X, Threads, YouTube or Facebook), shown next to
   their name. Comments show publicly only after Jonathan approves
   them — the form says so, so nobody wonders where theirs went.
   Updates from Jonathan's own social media (posted by his helpers)
   show in the same list, clearly labelled, with a link back to the
   original post. #}
<section class="comments-section" data-fade aria-labelledby="comments-heading"
  data-comments
  data-comments-post="{{ page.fileSlug }}"
  data-comments-lang="{{ site.language }}"
  data-comments-api="{{ site.commentsApi }}"
  data-comments-client-id="{{ site.googleClientId }}">
  {# Comments live in a glowing dropdown — shut by default, tap to open.
     The heading and the count stay visible when it is shut; the count
     text is updated by js/comments.js once the thread loads. Sign-in
     (Google button, interview session check) waits until the reader
     opens it — the Google button cannot render into a shut panel. #}
  <details class="comments-dropdown" id="comments-dropdown">
    <summary class="comments-dropdown__summary">
      <span class="comments-dropdown__title" id="comments-heading">Comments</span>
      <span class="comments-dropdown__count" id="comments-count">Loading…</span>
      <span class="comments-dropdown__chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
    </summary>
    <div class="comments-dropdown__body">
  <p class="comments-note" id="comments-note">Sign in with Google to join the conversation.</p>
  <div id="comments-signin"></div>
  <ul class="comments-list" id="comments-list" aria-live="polite"></ul>
  <form id="comments-form" hidden>
    <p class="comments-as" id="comments-as"></p>
    <label for="comments-text">Your comment</label>
    <textarea id="comments-text" name="text" rows="3" maxlength="1000" required placeholder="Write a comment…"></textarea>
    <label for="comments-social">Your social profile (optional)</label>
    <input id="comments-social" name="social" type="url" inputmode="url" placeholder="Link to your Instagram, X, Threads, YouTube or Facebook profile">
    <label for="comments-video">Video reply (optional)</label>
    <input id="comments-video" name="video" type="url" inputmode="url" placeholder="YouTube link — pasting a video makes it a video reply">
    <p class="comments-approval">Comments show here once Jonathan has had a look at them.</p>
    <button type="submit">Post comment</button>
  </form>
  <p class="comments-result" id="comments-result" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <noscript><p>Comments need JavaScript enabled.</p></noscript>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>
